# Your own sources are yours. This template tracks the machinery and the rules,
# never your library — you almost certainly do not want a gigabyte of PDFs in git.
# Delete these two lines if your raw/ is small and text-only and you want it versioned.
/garden/raw/*
!/garden/raw/README.md

# Transient staging tray. The permanent copy always ends up in raw/.
/garden/inbox/*
!/garden/inbox/README.md

# Search index, if you get as far as installing qmd (README Step 4). A rebuildable cache,
# never provenance — ALL of it, config included. qmd writes absolute paths into
# .qmd/index.yml, so a tracked copy points at this computer's home folder: on any other
# computer qmd indexes nothing and says nothing, and on a public repo it publishes your
# username. The extracted library text stays out too — on a public repo it would publish
# the full text of every paper you hold. Re-run the four Step 4 commands on each computer.
/.qmd/
/garden/.qmd/

.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
